WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.882
A recursive CTE has two parts.

00:00:02.882 --> 00:00:05.717
The anchor term starts the result.

00:00:05.717 --> 00:00:11.082
The recursive term refers to the CTE and finds the next level.

00:00:11.082 --> 00:00:14.537
UNION ALL combines the rows.

00:00:14.537 --> 00:00:20.482
The process continues until the recursive term produces no more matching rows.

00:00:20.482 --> 00:00:24.877
This is useful for hierarchies and parent-child structures.

00:00:24.877 --> 00:00:31.712
A CTE gives a name to an intermediate result so a complex query can be read in stages.

00:00:31.712 --> 00:00:40.037
Use it to clarify grain changes and major transformations, not simply to break every two lines into a new

00:00:40.037 --> 00:00:47.128
block. A useful CTE name describes what the rows represent, such as patient_totals or ranked_visits.
